  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `tests/support/stored_graph.rs` `impl[UnreadContents/NodeContents]/fn[format]` is a fenced commentary citation on an explicit function, so the built-in allows it. Its stated reason is substantive and matches the source.\n\n- `enum[UnreadContents]` has no variants, so no value of it can be built. `fn[format]` has body `match *self {}`, which has no case that could run, so no execution coverage is possible.\n- The commentary says storage tests supply no content values and reject node reads at the domain boundary. `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` agrees. It returns `UnreadContents` but panics with \"storage operations must not read graph contents\", so no `UnreadContents` value is ever created.\n- The citation excuses only this function's zero execution, which is the scope the built-in allows.\n- `fn[format]` has no {impl} or {test} reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant.",
